===== add_transition required ['clip', 'duration']
DESC: Makes an overlap at the HARD CUT before a clip and puts a transition on it — Clip ▸ Transition ▸ <kind> on a clip that abuts the one before it. The overlap is built out of material the two clips already have (the source before the incoming clip's in point, and after the outgoing clip's out point), so NOTHING else on the timeline moves and the pair's outer edges stay exactly where they were. duration is snapped down to whole frames and CLAMPED — to each side's available material, to the neighbours on the track, and to the overlap rule — so a request too long for the media lands shorter rather than failing; a request that clamps below one frame is refused. An affected track already outside the overlap rule is refused by that rule before fitting. align center takes half from each side (an odd frame goes to the incoming clip, and a side with nothing to give passes its share to the other), before takes it all from the incoming clip's head, after all from the outgoing clip's tail. kind absent uses the clip's stored kind if it has one and cross_dissolve otherwise; a stored transition keeps its curve and crossfade, a new one is eased at both ends and crossfades its sound. The incoming clip's actions move with its new first frame, so a zoom stays on the source frame it was drawn over. Errors when duration is not positive and when the clip is NOT at a hard cut, naming which of: no clip before it, a gap, an overlap that already exists (use set_transition or set_transition_duration for that one). With ripple true the overlap is made by MOVING instead — the sheet's Shift Clips Left button when neither clip has footage beyond the cut: no material is read and align is ignored, and the incoming clip plus every clip at or after the cut on every unlocked track slides left by duration, so the timeline gets that much shorter and no clip's source window changes. It is capped at half the shorter of the two clips and limited to the greatest whole-frame shift that leaves every moved track inside the overlap rule, including after clips cross; a clip on another track pushed into its neighbour gets a cross_dissolve; markers do not move.
