219	//! `set_action_end`'s graphic arm (format version 13, spec §11 G-34): the
220	//! door through which an action's `end` comes to carry
221	//! `graphic: {props: {<key>: <value>}, kinds: {<key>: <type>}}`.
222	//!
223	//! It is a door of its own and not a fifth `patch::Group` (G-32 (h)
224	//! stands): a graphic's keys are its MODULE's, not the vocabulary's, so
225	//! there is no template to walk. What a prop may hold is read from the
226	//! `schema` the op carries — the module's current revision, filled by the
227	//! app and never by a caller (G-4) — through `model_graphic.rs`'s
228	//! `check_typed`, the check `set_graphic` makes, under `graphic.props.<key>`.
229	//!
230	//! **This is the one end that IS range-checked** (§5.4's ends are not),
231	//! because nothing clamps a prop downstream: the engine reads no
232	//! `min`/`max`, and `actions_clamp.rs`'s `clamp_video` never sees `graphic`.
233	//! Every curve is monotone, so a ramp between two in-range ends stays in
234	//! range. Only the props a PATCH names are read; a stored end is never
235	//! re-checked, so a project whose module has since narrowed a range still
236	//! takes an edit to another prop.
237	//!
238	//! Each named prop's schema `type` is written into `kinds`, which is how the
239	//! evaluator (`actions_graphic.rs`) knows a colour from a string; a `kinds`
240	//! in a patch is read and discarded, so an end read back from `get_project`
241	//! can be sent again and no caller decides a kind. A prop the clip's own map
242	//! lacks starts from the schema's CURRENT default, appended in the same
243	//! edit (G-34 (d)). Maps change only by `insert` and `shift_remove`
244	//! (`model_graphic.rs`'s rule).
245	//!
246	//! A prop whose schema entry says `animate: false` is refused by name
247	//! (G-41): its module draws it whole, a count or a layout mode a ramp would
248	//! break. Like every check here it reads only a named, non-null prop, so an
249	//! end that named the prop before its module said so keeps animating it as
250	//! stored, and a `null` removes it. An `asset` is checked as `set_graphic`
251	//! checks it and switches at the action's end, as a string does; "no image"
252	//! in an end is `""`, since a `null` there removes (G-42).
